'' A UDT whose 'operator cast' yields text, into a type constructible from several text
'' types: fbc's pick and value, every line measured. The cast's exact type wins, then fbc's
'' own order (symbols/structpick.tiko TextCastRank_); tiko scored string, zstring and ustring
'' alike, the tie read as "no pick", and lowering took the chain's first constructor -- an
'' EMPTY ustring when that was the ustring one, an internal compiler error (TKO0994) when it
'' was a boolean one. Also: a ustring or wstring cast CONVERTED into a byval string (was
'' TKO0994), a text cast into 'byref as const zstring' (was the UDT's own bytes, so empty),
'' and a 'zstring ptr' cast into 'byval as const zstring ptr' (was TKO0698).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/udt-text-cast-ctor-pick.bas -o tests/codegen/udttextcastctorpick.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/udttextcastctorpick.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/udttextcastctorpick.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T1s=3[s1]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: F1=[s1]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T2s=5[s1]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T2u=4[u2]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T3u=7[u2]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T3z=7[z]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T4z=10[z]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T4w=8[w]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T5u=12[u2]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T5w=12[w]
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: T6p=14[p]
